    "explanation": "Driver D-19760 and rider R-42871: most of the record is agreed, but one fact this category's rule needs cannot be established from the evidence, so the case goes to a human reviewer.\n\nWhat is established. The driver reached Block 9, Selegie Road at 12:46:50 — the trip record's driver_arrived event, corroborated by the GPS trace (nearest fix 3.49 m from the pickup with 4 m reported accuracy, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius) — and cancelled at 12:53:20, 390 s later, after the 300 s free wait that ran from arrival and expired at 12:51:50 (POL-NS-21; EV-TRIP-06065, EV-GPS-06065). The payments ledger charged the 5.00 SGD policy fee, matching the policy exactly (POL-NS-22; EV-FARE-06065, fee_matches_policy=true). On 2026-10-09T13:32:20 the platform reversed it — 5.00 SGD refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver — after the rider's complaint (EV-TRIP-06065, event fee_reversed).\n\nWhat is not established. POL-NS-23 requires the driver, before cancelling, to have BOTH sent an in-app chat message AND placed an in-app call. The call is on the record (one in-app call at 12:49:20, unanswered, 22 s). Whether he messaged cannot be established: the chat log EV-CHAT-06065 is impaired — TRUNCATED_LOG, weight 0.6 — holding 1 of the 3 entries the trip record counts and nothing after 12:41:30, so it covers neither the arrival nor any part of the waiting window, which is exactly where a driver message would appear.\n\nRider's case (no driver message survives, so the message limb fails and POL-NS-23 voids the fee, leaving the refund standing): not accepted. A truncated export cannot establish that no message was sent, and POL-GEN-26 forbids reading an outcome out of absent evidence unless a rule says so. The limb is undecided, not failed. The rider's preserved 12:41:30 message (read 12:41:38) shows she was engaged and the channel was open, but it does not decide whether the driver replied.\n\nDriver's case (a 0.6-weight truncated export cannot prove a breach, so the fee stands and DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD is due): not accepted either. The same impairment that stops me finding a breach stops me finding compliance. POL-NS-22's compensation direction engages only where the fee stands, and whether it stands is precisely what POL-NS-23 leaves undecided, so its 5.00 SGD figure (fee_charged_sgd, driver_compensation_if_upheld_sgd) cannot be moved. The driver is right that the reversal was provisional, but neither POL-GEN-03 outcome can be reached on an undecided limb.\n\nGoverning clause. POL-GEN-26 names this fact — whether the driver messaged and called before cancelling — and directs escalation where the evidence that would carry it is missing or impaired. The chat log is impaired, so the case is escalated: no monetary outcome issues, both amounts are null, and the 5.00 SGD is held rather than released to either side.\n\nConfidence. Capped at 0.6 under POL-GEN-02(2): the deciding fact (the message modality cannot be established) is carried by the impaired chat log EV-CHAT-06065, weight 0.6, issue code TRUNCATED_LOG; no independent artifact carries it. This is above the 0.0 bar this no-show requires (POL-NS-26, POL-GEN-22: value 5.00 SGD, no fraud flag).\n\nNo referral issues. The fee charged is exactly 5.00 SGD, so POL-NS-22's amount check does not fire; POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not apply (on-demand trip with no scheduled time, and the driver did attempt contact); POL-NS-25's repeat no-show flag does not apply because rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is not present in the record.\n\nOpen question for the human reviewer: did D-19760 send an in-app chat message to R-42871 before cancelling at 12:53:20?"
